# sent_id = job15.23.1
# text = Πλαγκτοσύνῃ δέδμητο, καὶ ὡς ἀσύφηλος ἀλήτης Ἄκμηνος, καὶ ἄπαστος, ἐελδόμενός που ἐδωδῆς Πλάζετ' ἐπ' ἀλλοθρόων ἀνδρῶν δῆμόν τε πόλιν τε, Ἔλπεταί οἱ στυγερόν τε μόρον, καὶ νηλεὲς ἦμαρ Ἄγχι παρεστάμεναι, ὅτε μιν σκότος ἀμφικαλύψῃ Ταρβοσύνῃ καὶ πένθος ἔοι μέγα δεῖος ἐνόρσει, Κὰδ δ' ἕλεν ἰσχύσει, ὡς ὄρχαμος ἀλκὶ πεποιθὼς Ἄχριον ἐς πόλεμον κεκορυθμένος αἴθοπι χαλκῷ.
# source_parser = pyaegean grc-joint-v3
# reading_translation = He is worn down by wandering, and like a wretched, weary, famished vagrant longing somewhere for food he roams over the people and city of men of alien speech; he hopes that grim doom and the pitiless day stand near him, when darkness covers him about with terror and great fear of grief arises, and he is seized by strength, as a chieftain trusting in his might, armed in blazing bronze for the fierce war.
# literal_translation = By-wandering he-has-been-worn-down, and as wretched wanderer unwearying, and unfed, longing somewhere for-food he-was-roaming over alien-voiced men people and city and, he-hopes for-him grim and doom, and pitiless day near to-stand-by, when him darkness may-cover-about with-terror and grief may-be great fear may-arise, and down took by-strength, as chieftain in-might trusting fierce to war armed in-blazing bronze.
