# text = Ἠὲ τί οἱ μέγ᾽ ὄνειαρ ἀκήρατα σεῖο κέλευθα, Εἴπερ ἀμύμων αὐτὸς ἔης, καὶ ἀμύμονα εἰδῇς, Ἦ ὅτι σὴν ἀτίτην τρομέει, καὶ λοίγια ἔργα, Μή τι μιν ὑβρίζῃς, ἢ ἄλλό τι κύντερον ἔρδῃς, Τούνεκα νῦν σε ἔλεγξε, καὶ ἐν δίκῃ ἀντίος ἔστη;
# source_parser = pyaegean grc-joint-v3
# reading_translation = Or what great profit to him are your pure ways, even if you yourself were blameless and knew blameless things? Is it because he fears your punishment and your deadly deeds, that he reproves you, or does something else more shameless? Therefore now he has convicted you, and in justice has stood against you.
# literal_translation = Or what to-him great profit [are] undefiled thy ways, if-so-be blameless thyself thou-wert, and blameless thou-knowest, or because thy punishment he-fears, and deadly deeds, lest anything him thou-insult, or other anything more-shameless thou-do, therefore now thee he-convicted, and in justice opposite he-stood?
