# sent_id = job27.2.1
# text = Οὐ μὰ Θεοῦ ζωὴν, ὃς ἀκήρατος ἄφθιτος αἰεὶ Κάρτος αἰὲν ἔχει, δύναται δέ τε πάντα τελέσσαι, Ὅς βίοτον μοι ὄλεσσε, καὶ ἐξέλετο φρένας ἐσθλὰς, Ἠδὲ νόον μοι πικρὸν ἐνὶ στήθεσσιν ἔθηκεν, Οὔποθ’, ἕως ζώω, καὶ ἔχω ζωαρκέα πνοιὴν, Καί μοι θεσπεσίη μίμνει ἐν ῥίνεσσιν ἀϋτμὴ, Οὔ τις ἀκούσει ἐμεῖο κακὸν ἔπος, οὐδ’ ἀσύφηλον, Οὐδέ τ’ ἀτασθαλίη μοι ἀμείψεται ἕρκος ὀδόντων, Οὔτινα κλεψινόοισι παραπλάγξω φρένα μύθοις, Οὐδέ ποτε γλώσσης μειλίγμασιν ἠπεροπεύσω.
# source_parser = pyaegean grc-joint-v3
# reading_translation = By the life of God, who imperishable, undying, forever holds strength everlasting, and can accomplish all things, who destroyed my life and took away my noble mind, and put a bitter thought in my breast — never, as long as I live and have life-sustaining breath, and while a divine blast remains in my nostrils, will anyone hear from me a wicked word, or a reckless one, nor will transgression pass back through the fence of my teeth; I will not deceive anyone's mind with thievish words, nor ever beguile with flatteries of the tongue.
# literal_translation = Not by God life, who imperishable undying ever strength ever holds, and can also all-things accomplish, who life to-me destroyed, and took-away mind noble, and thought to-me bitter in breast put, never, while I-live, and I-have life-sustaining breath, and to-me divine remains in nostrils blast, not anyone will-hear of-me evil word, nor reckless, nor transgression to-me will-exchange fence of-teeth, no-one with thievish-mind I-shall-beguile mind with-words, nor ever of-tongue with-flatteries I-shall-deceive.
